now emails first reported by the new  york post  show frequent communication between the  american federation of teachers and  top cdc officials just days before the  invited administration released its  school reopening guidelines  in one email a teachers union official  writes it would be great to see the  insertion of some variation of the  following  in the event high community transmission  results from a new variant of sars cove  2  a new update of these guidelines may be  necessary  in at least two instances language  suggestions  offered by the union were reportedly  adopted nearly verbatim  into the final text of the cdc document  but the aft in a statement to fox news  saying quote  the aft represents 1.7 million educators  health care professionals and public  employees who spent the last 14 months  serving on the front lines of the kovid  19 pandemic  so naturally we have been in regular  touch with the agencies setting policy  that affect their work and lives  including the cdc in fact we contacted  the agency more in 2020 during the trump  administration  than we have during the biden  administration in 2021  but republicans say the report shows the  binded administration is putting  politics ahead of science  by consulting one of its largest donor  groups here's senator tom cotton on the  faulkner focus  a short time ago we shouldn't have a  politicized public health bureaucracy  like the cdc  answering at the beck and call of the  teachers unions we need  kids back in school and back in real  school not sitting in a classroom  doing a zoom session with teachers who  are not in the classroom  we need kids in schools with their  teachers now  carl welcome to you and i'd like to  start and get your thoughts on this to  begin with  now in these emails that have now been  published pursuant to a foia request  we know that the aft called the cdc a  quote thought partner  and that in those emails expressed that  they were grateful for the cdc's quote  genuine desire to earn their confidence  and that begs the question whether  confidence means donations  the aft and its affiliates have long  been one of the most reliable  and deep pocketed donor constituencies  of the democratic party  rising up to almost 20 million dollars  in donations in the 2020 election cycle  in fact the aft is ranked 27th  out of 22 000 in contributors  your thoughts carl yeah let's come back  to that money question in a minute  i thought it was disingenuous with the  aft how the aft  responded they're saying look first of  all we talked more to the  trump administration in 2020 than we've  talked to the biden administration in  2021 well maybe that's because  the trump administration was in charge  of this coven issue from february of  2020  through january 20th of 2021  and joe biden has only been in charge of  this from january 20th  through today so there's a lot more time  that they would be talking to the cdc  and the second and more important point  to my perspective is this  it's not just the cdc they're talking to  they have the white house included  in these emails including the office of  public liaison  when i was at the white house i was in  charge of that office the people who ran  it reported to me  that's your outreach group that's the  people who are talking to your allies  and associates  out there to try and advance your agenda  so let's not kid ourselves this is not  the aft the the teachers union talking  to some career government employed the  cdc  they were including the biden white  house in these discussions  subtly sending the message to the cdc  hey we got friends at 1600 pennsylvania  avenue  you better be doing what we suggest  which is laying the predicate for us to  have more schools  that are not holding in person in  classroom instruction  so i i thought that's a particularly  thuggish move and  you know you'll notice they glossed over  it they weren't just talking to the cdc  they were talking to the white house and  using the white house leverage to get  from the cdc  what they wanted that's exactly right  kaylee this was indeed a triad  in those emails and and when pressed by  jake tapper  the cdc director multiple times he said  specifically i'm quoting her  can you point to any scientific reason  for students in the united states  not to return to in-person classes  tomorrow  director wallensky could not or would  not offer a scientific explanation  right because there wasn't a scientific  reason there was a political reason  it was the influence of the teachers  union i thought the biden administration  followed the science they passionately  proclaimed that but in fact  they have the teachers union dictating  the science this is extraordinary i  think this is a huge scandal  we knew back in july when i stood at the  white house podium that schools  should be reopened the data showed us  that i said it multiple  times as did president trump and others  and here we are  down the road and the teachers union is  reviewing guidance  they actually got to review the guidance  there at the cdc  before it came out you have if you  listen very carefully to president biden  and his words he will say  we should probably reopen schools in the  fall he said that as recently as last  week  even though every teacher will have had  an opportunity to be vaccinated and  older children  over the age of 16 as well uh it is  incredible and  the disproportionate impact here falls  on young working moms we saw that new  york times op-ed today  which said the biggest gender issue of  our time  will be working moms who cannot go back  to work  who have young children and are forced  to stay home and we see that they're  going back into the workforce  at a much lower rate than men and  president biden you are directly  responsible for that gender and equality  gap we're seeing  kennedy as the new york times puts it  the biggest issue of gender equality in  2021  may well be whether schools return to  near normal in the fall  yeah and and that is especially true for  younger children children in preschool  and you know obviously preschools are  not beholden  by large to the department of education  and you know they have  been following some of this guidance as  well and they've been  very sporadically opening and serving  families  and when it comes to families you don't  hear about learning you don't hear about  parents  parents are left completely out of these  discussions it's really just  about this massive power grab from the  union  and here they are writing the language  for the cdc that's getting  inserted into their recommendations so  how instrumental was the aft  and writing some of the coveted relief  legislation that gave schools 130  billion dollars  up to 200 billion dollars that you know  most of it doesn't even get to the  schools for another three years  so yes they donated 20 million to  democratic  campaigns in 2020 and that's so they can  look over politicians shoulders  and write this legislation for them so  it benefits them completely when i say  them  i mean the teachers union i don't even  mean teachers it's definitely not  students it's not kids who are in most  need of the services that are provided  at school particularly mental health  and some of the the food  supplementation that is given to them on  a daily basis  from these public schools and they're  the ones who are completely  left out in the cold especially middle  schoolers and high schoolers they don't  care if they ever come back frankly  and carl we see that direct influence on  legislation obviously  i mean even thought with the greater new  york hospital associations they're  writing that immunity clause for  themselves that made it into new york's  budget  so back to the white house how is it  possible for them to maintain with a  straight face  that they are impervious to political  influence that they are only following  the science  when here now it is laid out in black  and white before our eyes  well kennedy touched on it the american  federation of teachers is one of the  most powerful  and most uh generous uh political givers  as you pointed out  they gave 19 million 900 3 000  in political contributions in 20 in the  2020 election cycle virtually all of it  to democrat candidates virtually all of  it just a handful of gifts to a handful  of republicans  think about this in the school funding  in the covent relief bill the buy  not the bipartisan bills passed last  year not the five measures that got wide  bipartisan support  we're talking about the biden  administration straight party line vote  129 billion dollars in edge  in in public education funding that  means for every dollar in campaign  contributions  they got six thousand four hundred and  eighty one dollars and twenty six cents  in covent relief money now why is that  important because the cdc in december  said we need to remediate the effects of  covet in oliver public schools  up to 422 dollars for each one of the 50  million  plus students in our public schools  which was roughly then 21 billion  dollars  and that's assuming that you remediated  the  the entire transportation system of the  schools which turns out to be far more  expensive  than remediating the classrooms  themselves and protecting the students  so all they really needed was 21 billion  dollars and kennedy's right  most of that money very little of that  money gets spent this year  out of the coveted relief bill the  remediation money gets spent  the rest of it gets spent over the next  decade in fact more money is spent in  the last six years of the decade  that is being spent this year in on  education including the remediation  efforts  so look this is a big giant expensive  gift  to the to the to the to the teachers  union and they got it in part because  they  they gave a lot of political money and  they provide a lot of political muscle  to democratic candidates  it's not pretty uh imagine what would  happen fill in the blank of if you did  that for a republican group that gave  political money  and you can imagine what the headlines  would be in the washington post in the  new york times  uh carl i'm just gonna to get in a quick  word on that and then we're gonna move  to  to what's happening with governor cuomo  that's breaking right now  but the thought of that being in the  last six years that spending that would  mean that the children who really paid  the highest price  educationally throughout the pandemic  some of them won't even be in school  still  right they'll be in this middle school  and high school grades they won't even  get to benefit from that spending  and look the biggest benefit to these  children is to get them back in the  classroom  the schools have gotten budgets for that  they've got their annual budgets get  them back in class  and that to me is just amazing that the  that the teachers union is trying to  find yet another excuse  to keep a generation of our young  children from  learning as they should and and and  reaching the goals that they need  in order to have a successful life what  is going to happen to this last  this lost year and they want to turn it  into more than a lost year  and have the authority to do so it's  like senator cotton said to me we were  talking about how you know the teachers  union basically just gave its homework  to the white house and they put some of  that in along with the cdc  right into their their new guidelines

